{
  "body_human_readable": "The Oklahoma City Thunder won the 2025 NBA Finals, defeating the Indiana Pacers in a seven-game series. This victory marks the franchise's first championship since relocating to Oklahoma City and their second title overall, the first being in 1979 as the Seattle SuperSonics.\n\nThe final game of the series was held on June 22, 2025, with the Thunder winning Game 7 with a score of 103-91. The Thunder's Shai Gilgeous-Alexander was named the Bill Russell NBA Finals Most Valuable Player. Gilgeous-Alexander, who was also the regular-season MVP, scored 29 points in the deciding game.\n\nThe Thunder had a dominant season, finishing with a league-best 68-14 regular-season record and winning a total of 84 games including the playoffs. The Pacers' efforts in the final game were hampered by a significant injury to their All-Star, Tyrese Haliburton, who tore his Achilles tendon in the first quarter of Game 7.",
